    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 416,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Burns Cottage\nBurns Cottage , the first home of Robert Burns is located in Alloway , South Ayrshire , Scotland . It was built by his father , William Burness in 1757 . Burns , Scotland 's national poet , was born there on 25 January 1759 . It is a simple two-roomed clay and thatch cottage and has been fully restored to become part of Robert Burns Birthplace Museum . The museum has a bust of Burns by Patric Park ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
