      "end": 426,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Burns, Oregon\nIn 1930 , logging in the mountains north of Burns led to the creation of Hines , a lumber company town , and the timber industry remained important to the local economy until the 1990s . In addition to ranching , a variety of private and public enterprises support the Burns -- Hines economy in the 21st century . Annual events include a migratory bird festival , the county fair , and a country music jamboree ."
